  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). Transitive pair: {跳|は}ねる can also be used transitively in some contexts. Pattern: Xが{跳|は}ねる (X jumps/bounces).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing action. {跳|は}ねている = 'is jumping/bouncing.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {ぴょんぴょん}{跳|は}ねる (to hop around)\n- {油|あぶら}が{跳|は}ねる (oil splatters)\n- {水|みず}が{跳|は}ねる (water splashes)\n- {髪|かみ}が{跳|は}ねる (hair sticks out)\n\nHOMOPHONE:\n- {撥|は}ねる - to reject, hit (different kanji)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {跳|と}ぶ - to jump (higher, more distance)\n- {弾|は}む - to bounce, spring back",
